ion  we have five unknowns with two equations  there's no way we're going to be able to  individually figure out what a or B or C  or X or Y is but maybe we can use what  we saw in the last example to solve this  and so we might want to do is rearrange  it so that we have the X's and Y's kind  of group kind of grouped together and  the A's B's and C's kind of group  together so let's try that out so let's  focus first on the A's B's and C's so we  have negative 9 a negative 9 B I'll go  and order alphabetical order negative 9  B and we have negative 9 C and I think  you see what's emerging negative 9 C and  then let's work on the x's and the Y's  and then we have negative 7x minus 7x  and then we have a minus 7y so minus 7y  so all I have done is rearranged this  expression here but this makes it in a  way or it makes it a little bit clearer  of what's going on here this these first  3 terms these first three terms I can  factor out a negative 9 and I get  negative 9 times a plus B plus C and  these second two terms I can factor out  a 7 minus 7 times X plus y and just to  verify if you wanted to go the other way  multiply this negative 7 times X plus y  you'll get this multiply a negative 9  times a plus B plus C distribute it  you'll get this right over here and so  this makes it a little bit clearer what  is a plus B plus C equal to well they  tell us right over here a plus B plus C  is equal to negative 1 this whole  expression is negative 1 this and at  least in the parentheses and what is X  plus y equal to let me do this in a new  color what is X plus y equal 2 well they  tell us right over here X plus y is  equal is equal to 7 so this whole thing  simplifies to negative 9 times negative  1 times negative 1 minus 7 minus 7 times  7 times 7 and so this is equal to or the  homestretch negative 9 times negative 1  well that's positive 9  and then negative seven times seven is  negative 49 so it's 9 minus 49 which is  equal to negative 40 and we are done
 

